@nova_moth79. Some monitoring tools (like CloudWatch) can be a bit slow for reacting to the kind of "oh no, I've just used 50 compute hours" situations. Instead of relying on a budget alert for a service, it's better to take a proactive approach and control your budget.

Tools like AWS Service Quotas allow you to set your own hard limits on resource usage. And, if you have a quota, you will never get a surprise bill from the cloud provider. Quotas are a kind of wall: hard and fast. Set them to the highest value you are comfortable with.

If you want something a bit more dynamic, consider a service like Atlas. This service is also a budget alert, but scanning every 5 minutes, so you can set a course correction in the first 5 minutes, rather than waiting 90 minutes for a billing alert.

